+# Data Model: Keel Config Risk Tier
+
+**Feature**: [specs/001-bench/spec.md](spec.md) · **Date**: 2026-10-26
+
+This feature is docs-only: it changes no runtime data, no database schema, and no wire type. The
+"model" below captures the **documentation entities** the spec names under *Key Entities* and the
+classification rules they encode, so the wording contract in [contracts/](contracts/) has a stable
+vocabulary to draw from.
+
+## Entity: Proportionality table
+
+The two-column mapping from "the change" to "what is asked", existing once in the Keel section of
+`AGENTS.md` and once in section 2 of `docs/process/DELIVERY.md`.
+
+| Attribute | Type | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `rows` | list[row] | Four rows, fixed order (lightest → expanded). |
+| `row.change_class` | string | The class of change this row covers. |
+| `row.obligation` | enum | one of: `task_record`, `three_line_card`, `full_card`, `full_card_plus_jpd`. |
+
+Fixed rows (unchanged except where FRs direct):
+
+1. change_class: `Docs, comments, inert config values, a one-line fix, a test-only fix` → `task_record`
+2. change_class: `A bounded code change on the direct route` → `three_line_card`
+3. change_class: `New public surface: a module, type, public function, dependency or test file` → `full_card`
+4. change_class: `Persistence, permissions, compatibility, security, external effects, runtime-affecting config` → `full_card_plus_jpd`
+
+### Changes specified by this feature
+
+- **Row 1 (`change_class`)** — FR-001 / FR-002: the config term MUST read as **inert** config
+  values with the qualifier "no observable runtime or security effect" attached, so that a bare
+  "config values" phrase does not route to this row (SC-003).
+- **Row 4 (`change_class`)** — FR-004 / FR-005: the list MUST include **runtime-affecting config**
+  alongside persistence, permissions, compatibility, security, external effects.
+- **Supporting prose** (immediately after each table) — FR-003: MUST state that a runtime- or
+  security-affecting config change requires the full card **and behavioural evidence of the
+  changed behaviour**, not merely parse or shape validation.
+
+All other rows, columns, and sections: semantically unchanged (FR-008).
+
+## Entity: Config value
+
+Any setting in a configuration surface (config files, policy rules, tool settings).
+
+| Field | Type | Validation rule |
+|---|---|---|
+| `value` | scalar | — |
+| `tier_class` | enum: `inert`, `runtime_or_security_affecting` | Determined **by effect**, not by file location. |
+
+**Classification rule (state transition for tier purposes):**
+
+- `inert`: changing the current value produces **no observable** difference in runtime behaviour,
+  timing, permissions, or external exposure → routes to row 1 (`task_record`).
+- `runtime_or_security_affecting`: changing the value produces an observable difference in
+  behaviour, timing, permission, or exposure → routes to row 4 (`full_card_plus_jpd`) and owes
+  behavioural evidence (FR-003).
+
+Applied per value-class; a mixed diff is lifted off the lightest tier by any non-inert value
+(Edge Case: mixed change). File format never downgrades the tier (Edge Case: config inside Markdown).
+
+**Not classified inert by this change alone**: a value no shipped code currently reads but which a
+documented contract says *may* be read in future (Edge Case: "inert" vs "looks inert") — the author
+classifies it and makes the call visible in the record.
+
+## Entity: Full card with behavioural evidence
+
+The obligation pair owed for `runtime_or_security_affecting` config.
+
+| Component | Content |
+|---|---|
+| `card` | The complete Keel card in the PR body (paths in scope, promise, proving command). |
+| `behavioural_evidence` | A command or test that observes the behaviour the config value changed; parse/shape validation alone is not sufficient (reuses the Journey-Proven Development definition). |
+
+## Relationships
+
+```text
+Config value --classified by effect--> tier_class
+  inert                       --> Proportionality table row 1 (task_record)
+  runtime_or_security_affecting -> Proportionality table row 4 (full_card_plus_jpd)
+                                   + Entity "Full card with behavioural evidence"
+Proportionality table exists twice: AGENTS.md (Keel §) | docs/process/DELIVERY.md (§2)
+  constraint SC-002: both tables must classify every probe identically
+```
