+
+### Edge Cases
+
+- **Mixed change**: a single diff contains one inert value and one runtime-affecting
+  value. The non-inert value lifts the whole change off the lightest row (risk is read
+  from what the change touches, not from how much it adds). The documents state the rule
+  per value-class; the author applies it to the whole change.
+- **"Inert" vs. "looks inert"**: a value that no shipped code currently reads but that a
+  documented contract says may be read in future is *not* classified as inert by this
+  change alone; classification remains the author's call, made visible in the record. The
+  documents define inert by effect (nothing observable changes at runtime or in the
+  security posture), not by where the value sits in a file.
+- **Config change that also edits prose**: a config value edited inside a markdown file.
+  If the value is inert, the change stays in the lightest tier (docs); if the value is
+  runtime-affecting, it takes the full card regardless of file type. File format never
+  downgrades the tier.
+- **Scope boundary**: the rule lives in exactly the two named tables and their immediate
+  supporting prose. No checker script, no `keel.yaml` policy rule, and no other document
+  is created or modified by this change.
+
+## Requirements *(mandatory)*
+
+### Functional Requirements
+
+- **FR-001**: The lightest row of the Keel proportionality table in the Keel section of
+  `AGENTS.md` MUST be limited to *inert* config values, stating that a config value
+  belongs there only if no observable runtime behaviour or security posture changes.
+- **FR-002**: The lightest row of the Keel proportionality table in section 2 of
+  `docs/process/DELIVERY.md` MUST carry the same limitation as FR-001, worded so that a
+  reader of either document arrives at the same classification.
+- **FR-003**: Both tables' surrounding prose MUST state that a runtime- or
+  security-affecting config change requires the full card and behavioural evidence of the
+  changed behaviour (not merely parse or shape validation).
+- **FR-004**: The expanded-route row of the table in the Keel section of `AGENTS.md`
+  (currently: persistence, permissions, compatibility, security, external effects) MUST
+  include runtime-affecting config in its list.
+- **FR-005**: The final row of the table in section 2 of `docs/process/DELIVERY.md`
+  (currently: persistence, permissions, compatibility, security, external effects) MUST
+  include runtime-affecting config in its list.
+- **FR-006**: The change MUST NOT create or modify any executable checker, validator, or
+  `keel.yaml` policy rule, and MUST NOT modify any file other than `AGENTS.md` and
+  `docs/process/DELIVERY.md`.
+- **FR-007**: Both documents MUST remain in English after the change, per repository
